Brazier is NOT TeaVM, and is renamed so that no consumer can confuse the two:
its Maven group, artifact names, Gradle plugin ids and project name all differ.
Java package names are deliberately left as org.teavm.*, because renaming them
would conflict on every file in every future merge from upstream, and a package
name is not the mark being separated.

Every file Brazier changes relative to upstream carries a modification notice,
and CHANGES.md lists the complete set. A gate in CI fails the build if any file
differs from upstream without being declared there, so that list cannot quietly
fall out of date.

Bugs found in Brazier are reported to Brazier. Do not report them upstream
unless they reproduce against unmodified TeaVM.

